From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zinc Authors <zinc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:45:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Zinc: Customizable phone toolbar with pinned extensions

The phone toolbar gets up to four customizable buttons (see the overlay
package org.chromium.chrome.browser.toolbar.zinc). Each button can be
pinned to any basic browser function and placed left or right of the
address box; the stock home, tab switcher and adaptive buttons are
replaced by them.

Extensions: upstream only hosts the extensions toolbar on ToolbarTablet.
Add the extensions stub to toolbar_phone.xml between the end buttons and
the app menu, let ToolbarManager create the ExtensionsToolbarCoordinator
for any toolbar layout, and have ToolbarPhone give pinned extensions only
the width the address box can spare (ZincToolbarWidthPlanner), so
overflowing extensions stay in the puzzle menu. Pin/unpin and reordering
use the upstream extensions menu, context menu and drag support.

ToolbarPhone also draws the new views into the toolbar texture capture,
hides them during URL focus with the other toolbar buttons, and keeps
their tint and ripple in sync with incognito and theme changes.

